## Commands

```bash
pnpm install        # install
pnpm check          # lint, format:check, typecheck, test (all packages)
pnpm run ci         # the CI task list on changed packages (--affected)
pnpm format         # vp fmt
pnpm agents:index   # regenerate docs/agents/index.md
```

Packages call `vp build/test/lint/fmt/pack` directly (Turbo caches); never `vp run`.
`scripts/ci-extra.sh` (seed): repo checks, run last in CI; keep fast.

## Rules

- Test first, then implement; verify with real output before saying done. Tests: `*.test.ts` beside
  source, from `vite-plus/test`; one package: `pnpm --filter <name> test`.
- One task per change; no drive-by refactors.
- Versions: exact pins in the `pnpm-workspace.yaml` catalog; `catalog:` in packages.
- Template-owned files (configs, workflows, `.claude/`) change via `splice update --all`; local changes go
  in seed files, `docs/agents/project.md` or a package's `AGENTS.md`.
- Never print, read or commit secrets (`.env*`, keys). Releases are tag pushes by a human: never publish,
  push tags or push the default branch; use a PR.
- The guard hook is a rail, not a sandbox: the real fix is a server-side branch ruleset.
- A hook `ask` is a denial in unattended runs: use the alternative its reason names.
- At most 2-3 parallel agents on barely overlapping files; note next steps in `docs/agents/project.md`.
- Sibling package: `"@scope/name": "workspace:*"`, then `pnpm install`.

## Ready for a PR

Branch `feat/<topic>`; commits `feat:`/`fix:`/`docs:`. `pnpm run ci`, one push, `gh pr create`, `gh pr merge --auto`.
